  "question": "The bank management system requirements are described as follows: The bank has multiple branch offices, and the name and address of each branch office are recorded. Each branch office has multiple customers, and each customer has a Customer ID, name, ID number, contact phone number, and email address.\nCustomers can open accounts at multiple branch offices, and each account has a unique Account number, Account type (Savings, Checking), balance, and open date.\nThe bank needs to record the transaction history of customers, including Transaction type (Deposit, Withdrawal), Transaction amount, Transaction time, and Transaction location.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0294\nCREATE TABLE `branch_office` (\n  `branch_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `branch_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `branch_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`branch_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `id_number` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_phone` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `email_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `branch_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`),\n  KEY `customer_ibfk_1` (`branch_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `customer_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`branch_id`) REFERENCES `branch_office` (`branch_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `account` (\n  `account_number` varchar(30) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `branch_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `account_type` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `balance` decimal(15,2) NOT NULL,\n  `open_date` date NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`account_number`),\n  KEY `account_ibfk_1` (`customer_id`),\n  KEY `account_ibfk_2` (`branch_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `account_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `account_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`branch_id`) REFERENCES `branch_office` (`branch_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `transaction_history` (\n  `transaction_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `account_number` varchar(30) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_type` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_amount` decimal(15,2) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`transaction_id`),\n  KEY `transaction_history_ibfk_1` (`customer_id`),\n  KEY `transaction_history_ibfk_2` (`account_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_history_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_history_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`account_number`) REFERENCES `account` (`account_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
